 ('MatrixBinding delegates logical tiling identity to shared Metadata','dims folds physical shape/tiling; row_first_tile/fused validate row-serving shape via Geometry.',[D+'matrix.rs',D+'cmma/launch.rs',D+'cpu_gemm/launch.rs'],'This is real shared physical-storage authority for tiled routines. Batch fragments are explicitly refused in tile(), stored tiles must match a stage or level via host cut_by before worker dispatch. dims still expects valid rank/tiling and subtracts2. row_major checks last stride1, not overall contiguity; actual row strides may legitimately remain pitched. Shared Launcher extent admission still external, so ignored-RHS-K suspicion remains qualified.'),
 ('QuantGemv is a new explicit packed routine outside Strategy enum','QuantGemvProblem/Blueprint/Bindings/Elems and public launch_ref own weight orientation and scale levels.',[D+'quant_gemv/base.rs',D+'quant_gemv/launch.rs',D+'quant_gemv/mod.rs',D+'strategy.rs'],'Packed weights are lhs[d_out,d_in], activation[rows,d_in], output[d_out,rows]; this is a real separate contract from general matmul and not an auto-selected Strategy arm. Problem reports block field/scale count; bindings remain separate operands. Launcher arg builder receives field/width and owns packed availability checks; problem validation itself only admits block/word tiling.'),
 ('QuantGemv source explicitly resets output inside every kernel call','Before contraction turns each unit zeroes the output window, then accumulating windows fold turn results.',[D+'quant_gemv/kernel.rs',D+'quant_gemv/base.rs'],'This is different from Q454 atomic benchmark once-only host allocation. One word of scales per unit turn and interleaved KB are stated in shared levels; blueprint.units indexes resulting list at3. Separate blueprint.grid and level derivation still require parity; groups*units must equal actual plane width. No device execution/precision receipt inferred.'),
 ('QuantGemv scale mapping combines common representation with local admission','Launch allows1..2 scale levels, each dimension full or1; global scale field must occupy a word.',[D+'quant_gemv/launch.rs'],'Block field is from problem; tensor scale dtype is a separate field checked even when only one level is bound. Weight/x/out extents are delegated to Launcher. No local max-units check in blueprint beyond closing plane, so forced many-plane admission relies on shared Launcher. Binding names/type args do not independently validate underlying GPU byte contents.'),
 ('Storage relayout has one bidirectional kernel and host launch owner','tile and untile share relayout_launch/relayout, delegating StorageLevels/Partitioning to cubek-tile.',[D+'storage.rs'],'Packed sources drop finest word tile and scale shape/strides into words; returned metadata describes values again. Host refuses already-tiled input or noncontiguous pack axis. Caller-supplied dtype/axes/packing validity still matters; empty axes, rank mismatch, word-alignment and width narrowing need qualification before claiming total Result contract. Untile supports plain values per docs; no implicit packed decoding promised.'),
 ('Tiled axes and printable labels have fixed-width limits','batch_axis maps usize to u8 then adds3; labels has six batch names.',[D+'operands.rs',D+'matrix.rs'],'Small ordinary tensor rank is assumed. More than six printed batch axes panics indexing labels; enough batch axes can wrap/overflow identity. These are format/domain followups rather than proved current product calls. The axes constants are genuinely shared among tiled routines.'),
 ('Autotune key has a separate shape reconstruction authority','Metadata logical-shape folding is shared but m/n/k extraction is copied and rank-coupled.',[S+'tune_key.rs',S+'definition/base.rs',S+'multi_level/routines/gemm/launch.rs'],'Q455 ties key bug to Q450 launcher migration, alongside Q446 CPU reference own-rank issue. StorageTileKey distinguishes tiled pieces/order and stride factors remain actual runtime alignment despite anchored dimensions. Tests read only equal-rank keys, storage order and alignment buckets; asymmetric-rank gap remains.'),
 ('Key bucketing deliberately merges shape policy but preserves alignment','Definition anchors m/n/k and uses anchored pow2/scale classification, while stride factors remain real.',[S+'tune_key.rs'],'This resolves interpreting fewer key buckets as inherently incorrect: launch still derives vector legality from real tensors. Batch sizes/quant scheme details are not key fields beyond layout/dtype/stride and storage; this may share strategy performance/admission across materially different shapes, requiring actual tuner/caller trace rather than assuming equivalent kernels. Q455 is a concrete dimension defect independent of intended bucketing.'),
